"tender": {
"description": "Leicester City Council are using EEM0037 - Door Entry Framework to find a suitable contractor to perform installations of GSM/4G door entry systems at sheltered housing schemes in Leicester City and ongoing maintenance for the life of the contract. General requirements include, but not limited to: \u2022 All wireless Video GSM/4G Door entry and access control equipment must be vandal resistant and from the same manufacturer (all-in-one solution) granting access to remote, secured and cloud-based management allowing INSTANT system updates. \u2022 All Door entry and access control equipment must have THREE years parts only manufacturer's warranty. \u2022 The manufacturers must provide the fully pre-programmed and \"ready to use\" system including key fobs in accordance with the Leicester City Council instructions. The initial contract award value is \u00a383,158.72. However, provision has been made for up to \u00a3250,000.00 of additional expenditure over the contract term to cover parts, replacements, and call-out fees, where required.",
